              "patch": "diff --git a/HANDBOOK.md b/HANDBOOK.md\nindex f1e28a82f16b24ad158b04df73b2b25256a98c52..8a5ca9e314a50db642cf9101f859a52c893ef84c 100644\n--- a/HANDBOOK.md\n+++ b/HANDBOOK.md\n@@ -538,7 +538,9 @@ release. Size from measurements of your own workload.\n ### 9.4 High availability\n \n The Coordinator is a single writer that holds state in memory; two\n-instances writing one workspace lose entries silently\n+instances writing one workspace lose entries. With the stores the\n+coordinators ship, the second writer's writes are refused and reported;\n+with a store that implements only `save`, the loss is silent\n ([SPECIFICATION.md §10.3](./SPECIFICATION.md#103-single-writer-requirement)).\n Run one active instance per workspace, partition workspaces or lock\n writes externally, and start a standby from the store on failover.\ndiff --git a/SECURITY.md b/SECURITY.md\nindex 7841e76512217dd8a65944045573c1765bae116d..4e245fbd33ab56185cd7747029a6713648c02c53 100644\n--- a/SECURITY.md\n+++ b/SECURITY.md\n@@ -290,9 +290,11 @@ head. It does not show that the log is complete. Whoever can write to the\n store can rewrite or remove entries and recompute every later link and the\n head, and the result still passes. A head that has been published, or\n anchored where that writer cannot change it, pins the log up to that point.\n-Two or more coordinator instances writing one store lose entries without any\n-error and re-link the chain, which then passes too, so each workspace needs a\n-single writer (SPECIFICATION.md §10.3).\n+Two or more coordinator instances writing one workspace lose entries, so each\n+workspace needs a single writer (SPECIFICATION.md §10.3). The stores the\n+coordinators ship refuse and report the second writer's writes. A store that\n+implements only `save` loses entries without any error and re-links the chain,\n+which then passes too.\n \n **Anchoring.** With `audit-scitt/1.0`, `audit.submit_to_scitt` builds one\n statement for each entry in the range it is given, the whole log by default,\ndiff --git a/SPECIFICATION.md b/SPECIFICATION.md\nindex afb56345ad227f2e8a13314c98025813d9247420..ab042f6d750a6b2866c9faf886460a8ee8f33402 100644\n--- a/SPECIFICATION.md\n+++ b/SPECIFICATION.md\n@@ -1354,22 +1354,31 @@ outright, because there is no chain to ask about.\n \n A Coordinator is a **single-writer** component. Its dispatch is serial, it\n holds workspace state in memory, and it computes each chain link from the\n-head it holds. The store interface is a persistence mechanism, not a\n-concurrency-control mechanism: `Store.save` is an unconditional write.\n-\n-Running two or more Coordinator instances against one shared store is\n-therefore **not supported**. A stale instance's write replaces a newer one\n-wholesale, so entries written by the other instance are lost, the chain is\n-re-linked from the surviving instance's head, and `audit.verify_chain`\n-reports `ok` on the result. The loss is silent and CHAP's own verification\n-will not reveal it.\n+head it holds. Running two or more Coordinator instances that write one\n+workspace is **not supported**.\n+\n+A write through `Store.apply` carries the new audit entries and names the\n+number of entries the Coordinator expects the store to hold for the\n+workspace already. The reference stores refuse a write that does not match,\n+and write nothing. With such a store a second writer is detected: the stale\n+instance's write is refused and reported, the entries the other instance\n+wrote are kept, and each later write by the stale instance is refused in\n+turn until it is restarted and reloads. The calls it answered in the\n+meantime took effect in its memory alone, and are lost when it stops.\n+\n+A store that implements only `Store.save` makes no such check: `save`\n+replaces the stored workspace wholesale. With such a store a stale\n+instance's write replaces a newer one, the entries the other instance wrote\n+are lost, the chain is re-linked from the surviving instance's head, and\n+`audit.verify_chain` reports `ok` on the result. The loss is silent, and\n+CHAP's own verification will not reveal it.\n \n Deployments needing more than one instance MUST serialise writes above the\n Coordinator, by partitioning workspaces across instances so that no\n-workspace is ever written by two, or by an external lock. Enforcing this in\n-the protocol, by making `Store.save` a compare-and-swap and dispatch\n-re-runnable against reloaded state, is a larger change than it appears and\n-is left to a later milestone.\n+workspace is ever written by two, or by an external lock. Detecting a second\n+writer at the store guards against a misconfiguration; recovering from one,\n+by re-running dispatch against reloaded state, is left to a later\n+milestone.\n \n ### 10.4 Checkpoints\n \ndiff --git a/conformance/differential/README.md b/conformance/differential/README.md\nindex 92ad88f2ff76f20059a41bb6cd3dbd089ec8af33..6e207224b2c90e30a6fb091adc6f50e05b1404de 100644\n--- a/conformance/differential/README.md\n+++ b/conformance/differential/README.md\n@@ -21,6 +21,11 @@ For each seed, `fuzz.py`:\n    request envelope, so a divergence in a *response* (for example a differing\n    artefact shape) passes the chain check and shows up only on response\n    comparison.\n+4. Replays the sequence into both references again, each on a SQLite file,\n+   and lapses every pending whisper. Each call writes only what it changed, so\n+   this checks that nothing was missed: a coordinator restarted on the file\n+   holds what the one that wrote it held, and the two files hold the same\n+   audit entries.\n \n Runs are reproducible: a seed plus deterministic ids and clock fully determines\n a run, so the seed *is* the regression corpus - a failing seed reproduces its\ndiff --git a/conformance/differential/fuzz.py b/conformance/differential/fuzz.py\nindex a4aa816b9662f6de5700fdf5e2d6bc53c5c6d16c..b565550633295fd17e3a1b18e4e373911d5e2c04 100644\n--- a/conformance/differential/fuzz.py\n+++ b/conformance/differential/fuzz.py\n@@ -23,6 +23,11 @@ what it received: a handler that writes into the request makes the recorded\n envelope differ from the signed one, and would otherwise be replayed into the\n other reference as though both had produced it.\n \n+Each seed is also replayed into both references on a SQLite file. Each call\n+writes only what it changed, so the check is that nothing was missed: a\n+coordinator restarted on the file holds what the one that wrote it held, and\n+the two references wrote the same audit entries.\n+\n Action selection reads the workspace as it stands: decisions go to tasks under\n review and to reviewers the review named, resumes go to paused tasks, handoffs\n are resolved by the participant they were offered to, votes come from\n@@ -42,12 +47,16 @@ from __future__ import annotations\n import argparse\n import json\n import random\n+import sqlite3\n import subprocess\n import sys\n+import tempfile\n from collections import Counter\n+from dataclasses import asdict\n from pathlib import Path\n \n from chap_coordinator import Coordinator, CoordinatorOptions\n+from chap_coordinator.storage.sqlite import SqliteStore\n \n _ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n _REPLAY = _ROOT / \"conformance\" / \"differential\" / \"replay.ts\"\n@@ -480,9 +489,15 @@ class Recorder:\n         return self.coord.get_workspace(\"w\").chain_head\n \n \n-def _replay_ts(envelopes: list[dict]) -> dict:\n+# Past every deadline the fuzzer sets, so a store replay lapses each whisper\n+# still pending, outside any call.\n+_LAPSE_AT = \"2100-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"\n+\n+\n+def _replay_ts(envelopes: list[dict], store: str | None = None) -> dict:\n     payload = json.dumps({\"options\": {\"defaultProfiles\": PROFILES},\n-                          \"workspace\": \"w\", \"envelopes\": envelopes})\n+                          \"workspace\": \"w\", \"envelopes\": envelopes,\n+                          **({\"store\": store, \"lapse_at\": _LAPSE_AT} if store else {})})\n     proc = subprocess.run(\n         [\"npx\", \"tsx\", str(_REPLAY)],\n         input=payload, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=str(_ROOT))\n@@ -491,6 +506,66 @@ def _replay_ts(envelopes: list[dict]) -> dict:\n     return json.loads(proc.stdout)\n \n \n+def _plain(coord: Coordinator) -> str:\n+    out = {}\n+    for ws_id, ws in coord.workspaces.items():\n+        data = asdict(ws)\n+        data[\"audit\"] = [e.to_dict() for e in ws.audit]\n+        out[ws_id] = data\n+    return json.dumps(out, sort_keys=True, default=str)\n+\n+\n+def _replay_py(envelopes: list[dict], store: str) -> tuple[list[dict], list[str], bool]:\n+    \"\"\"The Python reference on a SQLite file: responses, store errors, restart.\"\"\"\n+    options = dict(deterministic_ids=True, deterministic_clock=True,\n+                   enable_chain=True, default_profiles=PROFILES)\n+    errors: list[str] = []\n+    sq = SqliteStore(store)\n+    coord = Coordinator(CoordinatorOptions(\n+        **options, store=sq, on_store_error=lambda e, r: errors.append(str(e))))\n+    responses = [coord.dispatch(json.loads(json.dumps(e))) for e in envelopes]\n+    coord.check_whisper_lapses(\"w\", _LAPSE_AT)\n+    before = _plain(coord)\n+    sq.close()\n+    reopened = SqliteStore(store)\n+    after = _plain(Coordinator(CoordinatorOptions(**options, store=reopened)))\n+    reopened.close()\n+    return responses, errors, before == after\n+\n+\n+def _entries(path: str) -> list:\n+    con = sqlite3.connect(path)\n+    try:\n+        return [(seq, json.loads(data)) for seq, data in con.execute(\n+            \"SELECT seq, data FROM chap_entries WHERE workspace = 'w' ORDER BY seq\")]\n+    finally:\n+        con.close()\n+\n+\n+def check_stores(seed: int, rec: \"Recorder\") -> tuple[bool, str]:\n+    \"\"\"Both references on a SQLite file: nothing missed, the same entries.\"\"\"\n+    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n+        py_path, ts_path = str(Path(tmp) / \"py.db\"